  "design_rationale": "Evidence shows positive gain with 2-4s delay and long self-draining tau. u=0.4 drives y down to ~0.28 (E1) and from 0.62 down at -0.010/s (E12); u=0.6 drives y from 0.12 to 0.615 over 42s with slope falling 0.020 to 0.0074 (E5-E10); u=0 decays to ~0.12 with tau ~12-14s (E4); u=0.7 still rising +0.02/s at 0.5 (E2-E3). First-order fit to u=0.6 gives y_eq~0.82 tau~30s, while u=0.4 eq~0.25 implies strong nonlinearity/deadzone. Linearized deadzone fit y_eq=K*(u-dz) gives dz~0.30 K~2.7. Zero-crossing of slope at y~0.58: u=0.6 +0.0093/s vs u=0.4 -0.0104/s interpolates to u_eq~0.52 for 0.6. Hence feedforward ff=0.297+target/2.72 (~0.517 at 0.6). PI corrects residual: Kp=0.55 gives loop gain ~0.8-1.5 without exciting 3s delay, Ki=0.10 Ti~5.5s corrects 0.05 error in ~10-15s within 30s settling window. Integral gated to |e|<0.20 and clamped to +-0.25 leaves authority for ff error up to 0.25 (covers H6 0.55-0.70 uncertainty) while preventing windup during initial far approach. 1.5s EMA suppresses +-0.01 noise (std<0.02). 0.85 max and 0.75/0.80 safety caps prevent 0.9 hard cutoff given max rate 0.08/s.",
