  "change_summary": "Kept feedforward+PI structure but made it delay-tolerant: added latched slow-delay detector (~8s of drive without response), dual gain sets (fast Kp0.45/Ki0.055 vs slow Kp0.16/Ki0.012), slew limits (0.25/s fast, 0.04/s slow), Umax 0.82/0.68, slow feedforward trim, and predictive braking y_pred=yf+yd*Td gated on yf>0.55. This prevents integral windup and in-flight overshoot that caused 0.9+ violations under 22s deadtime while preserving nominal drive.",
  "design_rationale": "Old failure is classic deadtime instability: controller kept integrating/pumping while y was stale, then 22s of stored pump arrived at once. Fix must (1) detect deadtime online, (2) lower bandwidth so loop crossover <<1/Td, (3) limit rate and ceiling of u to bound in-flight energy, (4) brake early using y+yd*Td when already near band. Fast mode preserves nominal 2-4s performance; slow mode gives closed-loop Tc>>22s. Feedforward ~0.52 does most work so low slow gains still hold 0.6. Gated predictor avoids stalling far below target.",
  "diagnosis": "Deadtime/lag increased ~7x, gain/drain/sensor essentially unchanged. Nominal: E5 0->0.6 step flat ~3s then 0.0199/s rise; E2 0.4->0.7 lag ~2s. Post: E14 0->0.5 from rest flat 16s at 0.0001/s with noise <0.008; continuation E15 stays <0.01 until ~182.2s then breaks at 0.016/s. Total deadtime 159.9 to 182.2 = ~22.3s. Post-onset slope 0.016 at u=0.5 scales with nominal 0.02 at u=0.6, so actuator gain unchanged within ~20%. E13 u=0 fall starts immediately at -0.035/s high-level comparable to nominal E4, and zero reading/noise unchanged, ruling out outflow increase or sensor shift. Old PI with Kp0.55/Ki0.10 designed for 3s goes unstable with 22s, producing observed limit cycle 0.1-0.9 and hard violations.",
